+# feature:meshcore
+
+Dedicated MeshCore companion surface for the Raumata dual-protocol firmware.
+
+This module is intentionally separate from the Meshtastic node/message data
+model. MeshCore has its own ed25519 identities, channels and contacts, so mixing
+its records into the Meshtastic node database would create ambiguous identities
+and break assumptions in the existing repositories.
+
+## Transports
+
+MeshCoreKmp (`com.darkrockstudios:meshcore`) supplies the companion protocol,
+command queue, response parsing and high-level contacts/channels/messages API.
+Both transports are exposed to it as a `BleAdapter`:
+
+- **BLE** — `BlueFalconBleAdapter(BlueFalcon(context))`. MeshCore's BLE
+  interface sends one command per Nordic UART characteristic write.
+- **USB** — `UsbMeshCoreAdapter`, backed by the app's existing
+  `UsbRepository`/`SerialConnection`. MeshCore's USB CDC interface uses
+  `<` + uint16 LE length + payload for commands and `>` + uint16 LE length +
+  payload for responses, so `UsbMeshCoreConnection` adds/strips that framing
+  while presenting complete command payloads to MeshCoreKmp.
+
+USB permission is requested through the app's existing `UsbRepository`; BLE
+uses the app's existing Bluetooth permissions.
+
+## Structure
+
+| Path | Purpose |
+| --- | --- |
+| `MeshCoreAdapters.kt` | Platform transport interface + no-op adapter |
+| `MeshCoreRepository.kt` | Discovery, connection lifetime, channels/contacts, chat history |
+| `MeshCoreViewModel.kt` | UI state and actions |
+| `ui/MeshCoreScreen.kt` | Dedicated MeshCore tab |
+| `navigation/MeshCoreNavigation.kt` | Navigation 3 entry |
+| `androidMain/AndroidMeshCoreAdapters.kt` | Android BLE + USB adapters |
+| `androidMain/UsbMeshCoreConnection.kt` | MeshCore USB CDC framing |
+| `jvmMain`/`iosMain` | No-op adapters so the KMP module still compiles |
+
+## Usage
+
+Select the **MeshCore** destination in the app shell, choose USB or Bluetooth,
+scan, and connect. The screen shows channels and contacts; tapping one opens a
+chat pane with a message composer.
+
+## Limitations
+
+- MeshCore's BLE companion service must be enabled in the firmware. The current
+  firmware exposes MeshCore over USB; BLE MeshCore support is a separate
+  firmware series.
+- The app does not bridge MeshCore messages into the Meshtastic conversations
+  list. That requires the optional bridge described in the raumata design docs.
+- Only the companion subset implemented by the firmware is available: app
+  start, device query, contacts, channels, text, adverts and battery/storage.
+- The USB transport is Android-only; desktop uses the no-op adapter until a
+  desktop transport is added.
